\section{Experimental Evaluation}
\label{sec:eval}

\subsection{Setup}

All experiments were conducted on the k3d cluster described in
\S\ref{sec:impl}. We compare four systems:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{HPA}: Kubernetes HPA targeting 60\% CPU utilization
        per tier; scale-down stabilization window 60\,s.
  \item \textbf{IDQN}: Three independent DQN agents sharing the
        same state/action space as AURA but without a mixing network.
  \item \textbf{AURA-NC}: AURA with the hypernetwork-conditioned
        mixing network replaced by a simple element-wise sum of agent
        Q-values (no global state conditioning).
  \item \textbf{AURA}: Full system with QMIX mixing network.
\end{itemize}

Three workload profiles are evaluated:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Steady}: Constant 80\,req/s for 15 minutes.
  \item \textbf{Bursty}: 80\,req/s baseline with periodic $3\times$
        spikes of 90\,s duration every 5 minutes.
  \item \textbf{Step-increase}: Linear ramp from 80 to
        700\,req/s over 10 minutes, held for 20 minutes (motivated
        by the 10\,000-user load test in the system logs).
\end{itemize}
Each configuration was evaluated over three independent runs; mean
values are reported.

\subsection{SLA Compliance}

